  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Oceanographic In-situ Data Access",
  "description": "Interactive on-line data access to oceanographic in-situ data sets, which allows users to select data based on space, time, and keyword. Selected data can be viewed as user-customizable, on-the-fly plots, listed, or downloaded. Includes NOAA PMEL Pacific Ocean data observations from the tropics to the Arctic, and global data from the NODC World Ocean Database, served through the EPIC Web Browser and through OPeNDAP.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: NOAA/PMEL's EPIC system was designed for management, display and analysis of oceanographic and meteorological in-situ data with gateways to the web, popular analysis tools and the Internet. Web access is available at http://www.epic.noaa.gov/epic/ewb/. Most recently, OPeNDAP (formerly called DODS) access is available for OPeNDAP in-situ data clients at http://www.epic.noaa.gov:10100/dods.",
